-- title:
--   Conditional defect totals satisfy pair and triangle bounds
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, $I=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, $E=I\times\{0,1\}$, and $\Omega=\mathcal P(E)$. Let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean oracles on subsets of $I$. Write $R(S)$ for the natural-number value of the paired-rank routine with parameter $r$ and these oracles, and $d(S)=n-R(S)$ with subtraction truncated at zero. Let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids with ground set $I$ and common rank $r$, and assume $o_j$ returns true exactly on independent sets of $M_j$, for $j=1,2$. A transversal selects one label from each pair; let $T$ be this class. For distinct $i,k\in I$, let $D_{ik}$ be the class having pair $i$ empty, pair $k$ full, and every other pair singly occupied. All other states are invalid. For $q>0$ and positive rational multipliers $w_{ik}$, define $C(q)=\sum_{S\in T}q^{d(S)}$, $D_{ik}(q)=\sum_{S\in D_{ik}}q^{d(S)}$, and $\lambda(S)=q^{d(S)}$ on $T$, $\lambda(S)=w_{ik}q^{d(S)}$ on $D_{ik}$, and $\lambda(S)=0$ on invalid states. Let $Z_w=\sum_S\lambda(S)$ and $\pi(S)=\lambda(S)/Z_w$. Assume $q\le1$. Let $\sigma:I\to\{\mathrm{none},0,1\}$ be a partial assignment. A state respects $\sigma$ when each assigned pair contains exactly its selected label. Write $C_\sigma$ for the sum of $q^{d(S)}$ over respecting transversals, and $D^\sigma_{ik}$ for the sum over respecting states in the ordered-defect class with pair $i$ empty and pair $k$ full. For distinct unassigned $i,j$ and pairwise distinct unassigned $i,j,k$, respectively, $$4D^\sigma_{ij}D^\sigma_{ji}\le C_\sigma^2,\qquad D^\sigma_{ij}D^\sigma_{jk}\le C_\sigma D^\sigma_{ik}.$$
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ConditionalDefectCoefficientBounds.lean#L38-L113

